WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
In 1931,

00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:02.567
a crew looked out

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.000
after a blizzard and found

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:04.933
the ship they had left

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.000
in the ice was gone.

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:07.700
They assumed it had sunk,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.500
but local hunters soon

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.000
spotted the
abandoned steamer

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.500
near the Alaskan coast.

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:14.267
Over the following years,

00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:16.067
people saw and sometimes

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:16.967
boarded the ship

00:00:16.967 --> 00:00:18.367
without a crew as it

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:19.933
drifted with
Arctic pack ice.

00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:22.067
The latest company archive

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.233
record dates to 1969,

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:26.767
decades after the
ship was abandoned.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.967
The case documents an
extraordinary drift,

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:31.967
not a supernatural
ghost ship.

00:00:32.433 --> 00:00:34.367
Its final fate
remains unknown.
